  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "President Prabowo Subianto is set to formally submit two candidates for the vice presidency to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) on November 25. The assembly has initiated a rigorous verification process, with a dedicated team split into three working groups tasked with performing comprehensive field checks on the nominees. The selection process has triggered significant political discourse, with some observers advocating for candidates representing diverse regional interests. Meanwhile, the Gerindra Party has publicly countered allegations of impropriety directed at Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, one of the figures frequently discussed as a potential candidate, characterizing the claims as politically motivated attacks. The Corruption Eradication Commission (KPK) has also expressed readiness to assist the MPR in verifying the data provided by the prospective nominees to ensure transparency and accountability throughout the selection proceedings.",
